  "conclusion": "No blocking visual defect found in these final screenshots; 1382 is not a blank original image.",
  "observations": [
    "F2 quotes success 50%, 10 turns, durability -2 and noise 2 for precision picking; prying quotes a rusty knife, 30 turns and durability -5. The interface explains failure costs and the separate opening action.",
    "Yellow failure and green success logs are readable; the tall original closed-door frame remains after unlocking, then the original diagonal open leaf appears after the separate opening action.",
    "The original lockpick hook and L-shaped wrench are readable in its 1x2 bag footprint. Durability lines remain visible. Exact durability values are corroborated by existing state JSON, not inferred from pixel bar length.",
    "The four original shade variants are all visible in the unobstructed world screenshots. Their fixture explicitly marks them as met and freezes their next actions; this is not a claim about normal new-game knowledge or loadout.",
    "At 1366x768 the reviewed inventory, HUD, needs and log fit. No small-screen F2 screenshot is in this review set, so this review does not claim that an unseen small-screen F2 layout was checked.",
    "Both common titles retain the original art and complete start button at scroll zero; recorded bottom bounds are 880.28125 at 1440x1080 and 714.28125 at 1366x768, with both recorded center hit tests true.",
    "1382 appears partially black in view_image, but the original F2 panel, quote panel, visible HUD right section and status pixels are exactly byte-identical to 1381. Other original RGB counts also show the map and log retained. The image was neither brightened nor edited.",
    "This visual review and reading existing state artifacts do not replace the separate Native whole-world comparisons, save roundtrips or full regression tests."
  ],
